      "message": "Sorry for commenting on an old CL, but I\u0027m trying to understand the behaviour of critical services in the context of b/410865568.\n\nWhat is the meaning of `off` for argument `window` (used as default value for `zygote` processes)? I\u0027m asking because it\u0027s not documented in [`init/README.md`](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/system/core/+/1202249/13/init/README.md).\n\nLooking at [the parser\u0027s code](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/system/core/+/1202249/13/init/service_parser.cpp), it looks like `off` is meant to cancel the critical nature of the service; is this interpretation (which matches the current implementation) correct? Or was `off` meant to mean \"infinite window\" (which would match the interpretation and changes made in pa/3195585)?",
